Timing 1: A slow, continuous movement into the final pose. This would lack impact. Timing 2: A very quick transition to the flexed arm pose (low duration), followed by a slightly slower, deliberate head turn and torso lift with a long hold time. Winner: Timing 2, because the sharp contrast between the fast flex and the proud hold makes the gesture more dynamic and readable.
